mdeal@morgan.ucs.mun.ca (Michael Deal) writes:

>It's basically a God mode for debugging and experimenting where you can
>do anything you want.  To get into it, type nethack -uWizard -D.

Some machines are picky about the capital W, you might try a lower case
w, perhaps preceded by a space. Also, if you are playing on a mainframe
and are not the one who originally installed the game, wizard mode
might not work for you. In this case, you can always try:

nethack -X

which starts a game for you in exploration mode. This is about the same
as entering "X" while playing. The only difference is that when you
start a new game in exploration mode, you will start out with a wand of
wishing, which you don't get when entering this mode from the game
itself.

Of course, this is all mentioned in the Guidebook that comes with any
official version of NetHack.

